    "result_text": "The mapper wires `householdId` in both directions. The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature in this Spring Boot PetClinic app, keeping each piece of logic in a small, single-responsibility unit and reusing the existing household-matching rule.\n\n**What the change does:** When a `POST /api/owners` request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, the create is allowed even though an owner with the same last name and address already exists (existing behavior), and now the joining owner plus every existing owner in that household are stamped with the same stable `householdId`, which is returned on the owner.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` string to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto.getHouseholdId()`).\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `household_id` column. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the explicit column was required.\n- **`rest/validation/HouseholdKey.java`** (new) \u2014 the single source of truth for household identity: canonicalizes `(lastName, address)` (case-insensitive, collapsed whitespace) into a comparison key.\n- **`HouseholdDuplicateValidator.java`** \u2014 refactored to reuse `HouseholdKey` instead of its own private `normalize`, so duplicate detection and id assignment can't drift apart.\n- **`rest/assignment/HouseholdIdGenerator.java`** (new) \u2014 pure function deriving the stable `HH-<12 hex>` id from the household key (mirrors the existing `CustomerCodeGenerator`).\n- **`rest/assignment/HouseholdRegistrar.java`** (new) \u2014 orchestrates enrollment: stamps the joining owner and back-fills the shared id onto existing housemates that lack it, keeping this persistence logic out of the controller.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 calls the registrar on the `sharesHousehold` path before saving; the controller stays a thin orchestrator.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nBecause the id is a deterministic hash of the normalized last name + address, it's genuinely \"stable and shared\" \u2014 the same household always yields the same identifier, even across restarts.",
